\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces On the left, four selected non-disruptive shots incorrectly identified as disruptive by the CNN. Shots 176423 and 177030 feature a drop resembling a disruption, thereby confusing our model, while shot 178463 appears to be garbage data given that the current peaks at $\approx \qty {0.02}{\mega \ampere }$ (\ref {sub:false_positives}). On the right, four selected disruptive shots incorrectly identified as non-disruptive by the CNN. Each shot lacks the characteristic drop to zero that typically identifies a disruption, while shots 180501 and 177403 appear to be erroneously labeled and lack an evident disruption (\ref {sub:false_negatives}).}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cnn_errors}{{3}{3}{}{figure.3}{}}
\newlabel{current_norm}{{3}{3}{}{equation.3}{}}
\newlabel{fbeta}{{4}{3}{}{equation.4}{}}
